From: SamuriHL <samurihl@msn.com>
Subject: amdv: auto-clear the DV VSIF hold at core teardown

dolby_vision_vsif_hold (patch 0002) is released only by userspace at disc
-session end. While set it swallows *every* DOVI->non-DOVI VSIF teardown,
and enable_amdv(0) - the definitive "DV core off" path taken on stop /
return-to-GUI - does not clear it. So if userspace ever fails to drop the
flag (player crash, abnormal stop, or a non-DV title started inside a held
session without the release call), the SDR teardown stays swallowed and the
sink is left with BT.2020 + the Dolby VSIF signalled over SDR/GUI pixels,
with no watchdog to recover.

Add a self-healing clear: enable_amdv(0) calls amdv_clear_vsif_hold(), which
drops both the hold request and the active latch. A disc-session segment swap
keeps the core enabled and never calls enable_amdv(0), so the hold still
survives the gaps it was written for; only a genuine full teardown clears it.

--- a/drivers/media/enhancement/amdolby_vision/amdv.c
+++ b/drivers/media/enhancement/amdolby_vision/amdv.c
@@ -186,8 +186,22 @@
 static bool dolby_vision_vsif_hold;
 static bool vsif_hold_active;
 module_param(dolby_vision_vsif_hold, bool, 0664);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(dolby_vision_vsif_hold, "\n dolby_vision_vsif_hold\n");
+
+/* Self-healing release for the disc-session VSIF hold: called from
+ * enable_amdv(0) so a full DV-core teardown (return-to-GUI / stop) is never
+ * left with the hold latched when userspace failed to clear it (player crash or
+ * abnormal exit). A stuck hold otherwise swallows the DOVI->SDR teardown and
+ * leaves BT.2020 + the Dolby VSIF signalled over SDR/GUI pixels.
+ */
+void amdv_clear_vsif_hold(void)
+{
+	if (dolby_vision_vsif_hold)
+		pr_dv_dbg("clear stale VSIF hold at DV teardown (holder missed release)\n");
+	dolby_vision_vsif_hold = false;
+	vsif_hold_active = false;
+}

 static bool amdv_efuse_bypass;
 module_param(amdv_efuse_bypass, bool, 0664);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(amdv_efuse_bypass, "\n amdv_efuse_bypass\n");
--- a/drivers/media/enhancement/amdolby_vision/amdv.h
+++ b/drivers/media/enhancement/amdolby_vision/amdv.h
@@ -799,6 +799,7 @@
 extern bool force_stb_mode;
 extern unsigned int debug_dolby;
 extern unsigned int dolby_vision_flags;
+extern void amdv_clear_vsif_hold(void);
 extern uint amdv_mask;
 extern bool dolby_vision_on;
 extern bool amdv_core1_on;
--- a/drivers/media/enhancement/amdolby_vision/amdv_hw.c
+++ b/drivers/media/enhancement/amdolby_vision/amdv_hw.c
@@ -6457,6 +6457,7 @@
 	if (!enable) {
 		if (dolby_vision_flags & FLAG_TOGGLE_FRAME)
 			pr_dv_dbg("clear stale TOGGLE_FRAME at DV teardown (bypass path missed gated clear)\n");
 		dolby_vision_flags &= ~FLAG_TOGGLE_FRAME;
+		amdv_clear_vsif_hold();
 	}
 }
